  "cah3Note": "CAH3 (subject-level) landed only for disciplines named by this repo's existing content-pack directories (content/context-packs/: banking-and-finance, criminology, project-management, psychology, sports-journalism; baseline excluded, not a subject), per Prompt 67 ruling 3. Full CAH3 in v1.3.4 has 167 entries; this file carries only the four above. No CAH3 code named 'criminology' (or any crime/justice/policing term) exists anywhere in CAH v1.3.4 — checked directly against this file's own source CSV, grep for 'crim', 'justice', 'polic' under CAH15 (social sciences) and CAH16 (law) — so criminology is deliberately represented at CAH2 only (CAH15-01, sociology/social policy/anthropology, already present above as it is one of the complete CAH2 set) with no CAH3 leaf; inventing one would violate ruling 3's 'do not invent'. project-management has no CAH3 term of its own either (checked: CAH17-01's nine children are business and management (non-specific), accounting, tourism/transport/travel, marketing, human resource management, others in business and management, finance, business studies, management studies — no 'project management'); CAH17-01-01 (business and management, non-specific) is landed instead, matching the existing source-kb.json qaa/business-and-management-2023 entry's own collapsed classification, which the project-management context pack draws on.",
